// Biome is retained for ONE job: formatting `.astro` files. Everything else
// (JS/TS/JSX/TSX/JSON/CSS formatting, and all linting) moved to oxfmt + oxlint.
// See OXC_MIGRATION.md.
//
// IMPORTANT, and easy to misread: biome 2.5 formats ONLY the `---` frontmatter of
// an `.astro` file. The HTML template, `<script>` blocks and `<style>` blocks are
// left byte-identical. Astro templates are therefore unformatted by any tool in
// this repo -- exactly as they effectively were before this migration, since
// biome never formatted them either. oxfmt refuses `.astro` in every mode.
//
// Invariants:
//  1. `files.includes` MUST stay scoped to `**/*.astro`. Unscoped, biome fights
//     oxfmt and the two reformat each other's output.
//  2. The formatter options here MUST stay identical to `.oxfmtrc.json`, or the
//     `.astro` frontmatter drifts from the `.ts` files beside it. This repo is
//     "Family A" (printWidth 80 / double quotes / semicolons), which is exactly
//     biome's own default, so no `javascript.formatter` block is needed --
//     only `indentStyle`, whose biome default is `tab`.
//  3. `$schema` MUST match the exact pinned @biomejs/biome version or biome warns
//     on every invocation.
//  4. `biome format .` checks (.astro count + 1) files. The +1 is this file, which
//     biome always formats regardless of `files.includes` -- which is why
//     `.oxfmtrc.json` must ignore `**/biome.jsonc`.
{
  "$schema": "https://biomejs.dev/schemas/2.5.6/schema.json",
  "files": {
    "includes": ["**/*.astro"]
  },
  "formatter": {
    "enabled": true,
    "indentStyle": "space"
  },
  "linter": { "enabled": false },
  "assist": { "enabled": false }
}
